Package: stabPCA
Title: Reproducibility of Principal Components from the Eigenvalue Spectrum
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("César", "Galindo", email = "jcgalindo@up.edu.mx", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Enrique", "Hernández-Lemus", role = "aut"))
Description: Predicts which principal components of a correlation matrix are reproducible, from the
    eigenvalue spectrum alone. The fluctuation of a sample eigenvector is a sum of inverse squared
    eigenvalue gaps (Anderson, 1963) <doi:10.1214/aoms/1177704248>; it gives the expected overlap between
    components computed on two halves of the data, groups components that mix into subspaces, and gives
    the number of observations needed for a target reproducibility. Complements the significance tests
    of the 'sigPCA' package, whose input it accepts.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/IvliCaesar/stabPCA
BugReports: https://github.com/IvliCaesar/stabPCA/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: stats, graphics
Suggests: sigPCA
